  "kultivator.screen.help.ekonomi_kota": "All towns count money in NB (1 PK = 2 NB). Each price is multiplied by one town factor per category; it rises when stock runs low, with festivals or war, and falls with plenty. You can buy or rent houses at the Land Office (a few at most), rent a stall and open a shop, store goods in a Warehouse, take Trade Contracts, invest in townspeople's businesses and hold an office in town. Income from each source is capped per week to keep the economy fair; the Week tab of My Houses and Businesses shows what is left.",
  "kultivator.screen.help.ekonomi_kota.title": "Town Economy",
  "kultivator.screen.help.kehidupan_kota": "Towns live by a calendar: morning markets, the night watch, festivals, travelling troupes, weddings and funerals. The Town Book (World > Town) summarises residents, beds, the week's births and moves, the mayor, the next events, the plots being built and the news you heard there. News spreads by word of mouth and may be embellished; ask who said it to trace the source. Chase a pickpocket within 30 seconds; follow the night-watch rhythm or the puppet gong with a right click.",
  "kultivator.screen.help.kehidupan_kota.title": "Town Life",
  "kultivator.screen.help.kota_tumbuh": "New town buildings rise in stages on plots: foundation, frame, walls, roof, furnishing. Each stage needs materials (wood, stone, tiles, paper, cloth), a work crew and enough Prosperity. You may sell materials from your bag to a plot or donate money; the biggest donor's name goes on the sign. Officials of rank 4 and above choose the next plan. A badly damaged town is rebuilt only when the damage is real.",
  "kultivator.screen.help.kota_tumbuh.title": "Growing Towns",
  "kultivator.screen.help.sekte_kota": "A sect with a hall can protect a town by pact: tribute every week, guards from its disciples, and a Defend the Town call when the town is raided. A recruiting office takes rooted children of that town after a root test and the family's consent. Branches (a pill shop, a training hall, a clinic) give the town services and the sect influence. See also Sect > Territory.",
  "kultivator.screen.help.sekte_kota.title": "Sects in Town",
  "kultivator.screen.help.warga": "Every townsperson has a name, age, job, temperament, habits and memories of you. They are born, marry, grow old and die; those with a spiritual root can be invited to a sect if their family consents. Talk to someone to open a conversation: choose a line and a tone (Shift + 1 to 6), ask for news or directions, and give a gift once every few days. The Bond tablet opens the Townsperson Card: memories, debts, family, friends and the Family Tree. A good impression opens loans, work and franker news; a bad one closes them.",
  "kultivator.screen.help.warga.title": "Townspeople",
